  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>Quranic Grammar is free. You can read the lessons, use the tools and share links to any page. By using the site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use it.</p>

  <h2>What you may do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Study from it, and use it to teach others, for free.</li>
    <li>Quote short parts with a link back to the page they came from.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What you may not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sell the content, or copy the whole site or a whole course somewhere else.</li>
    <li>Overload the site with automated requests, or try to break into it.</li>
    <li>Use the feedback form to send spam or abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you want to use more than this allows, ask us through the <a href="/about/#feedback">feedback form</a>.</p>

  <h2>The content can be wrong</h2>
  <p>The lessons, word-by-word parses and explanations are written to help you learn, and we check them with care, but they can contain mistakes. Some surah pages say plainly that their explanations have not yet been checked against a classical i'rab book. For anything that matters, such as a ruling, a recitation question or a formal exam, ask a qualified teacher. If you find a mistake, please tell us.</p>

  <h2>Quran text and word data</h2>
  <p>The Quran text follows <a href="https://tanzil.net/" rel="noopener">Tanzil</a>. Word-by-word data comes from the <a href="https://corpus.quran.com/" rel="noopener">Quranic Arabic Corpus</a> by Kais Dukes, under the GNU General Public License. Recitation audio is by Mishary Rashid Alafasy, served by <a href="https://everyayah.com" rel="noopener">everyayah.com</a>. These keep their own licences and terms. The English meanings on this site are our own plain-English wording, not a translation of the Quran.</p>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>The site is provided as it is. We do not promise it will always be available or free of errors, and we are not responsible for loss caused by using it or by a site we link to.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>How we handle your data is explained in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may change these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed. Using the site after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

